R=[]
R.append(scoped_record('c0873','lancer-thirdcomm-metropolitan-core','Lancer — Union’s Third Committee Core','Lancer','Implemented Metropolitan necessities guarantees supported by printing',['tabletop'],
 'Published Lancer Third Committee setting','The functioning Galactic Core during established Third Committee government','Living human Metropolitan residents in Core settlements implementing the Pillars',
 ['Every member nation or remote Diasporan world','Harrison Armory and the Baronies as identical to Core society','Union’s aspirations as proof of implementation everywhere'],
 'Union’s developed Core combines printing and large-scale technological production with a material floor covering food, water and shelter. The Utopian Pillars make that floor a right, and the reference distinguishes their strong Metropolitan implementation from the unfinished project across the Diaspora. Guarantees therefore lie near the secure end for this selected Core population. The point does not turn every world nominally aligned with Union into an accomplished utopia.\n\nUnion is described as communal and post-capital, but the short references do not establish ordinary humans’ final ownership and override powers across the whole Core. Control remains unresolved, with a shared-human regime as the provisional classification rather than an automatic numeric conclusion from government rhetoric. Printing systems and nonhuman assistants do not themselves establish AI sovereignty. Residents still undertake research, administration, art, care, service and useful production. Freedom from survival wages, and the right to just labor, do not establish how many people undertake none of those activities. The nonworking fraction remains unknown.',
 [-.9,None,None],[[-1,-.6],None,None],
 ['The material Pillar, strong Metropolitan implementation and explicit printing/mass-production support establish the scoped floor; uneven Diaspora enforcement is excluded.','Communal/post-capital institutions suggest a shared-human regime but do not establish final ownership/override powers; no autonomous NHP sovereignty is inferred.','Voluntary or civic useful work continues; the right to necessities is not a participation census.'],[P+'union',P+'pillars',P+'printing'],2,alternatives=[1]))
R.append(scoped_record('c0878','dyson-program-virtual-homeland','Dyson Sphere Program — The virtual Homeland','Dyson Sphere Program','Active uploaded humanity sustained by automated physical energy production',['game'],
 'Game introductory premise and represented COSMO infrastructure','Established uploaded Homeland while engineers expand its sustaining energy supply','Active human-derived uploaded consciousnesses in the Homeland',
 ['Inactive data backups','Icarus as an independent nonhuman citizen','The player’s factory as proof of an unrelated ordinary organic society'],
 'Humanity’s virtual Homeland is an active populated environment whose computing demand is supplied through physical industry. The introductory guidebook, reproduced in a labeled community transcription, explicitly identifies uploaded human consciousnesses; the official description corroborates CentreBrain, COSMO and automated stellar-energy production. Continued support of those residents is the qualifying mechanism, rather than the mere possibility of a simulation. Guarantees receive a cautious favorable estimate because operating substrate is provided, while expanding demand and energy dependence limit security.\n\nCOSMO sends engineers through remotely controlled mecha to build the sustaining industrial system. This shows human-derived agency, but does not establish ownership or ultimate allocation authority inside the Homeland. CentreBrain’s name alone does not make it an autonomous machine sovereign, so control remains unresolved. Digital residents are an explicit human-derived proxy, and inactive backups are excluded. Engineering, design, science and useful creation continue in physical and virtual forms. The premise gives neither a resident activity census nor a universal exemption from all contributions; nonworking remains unknown.',
 [-.5,None,None],[[-.85,.15],None,None],
 ['The active uploaded Homeland depends on an implemented computing environment and COSMO’s automated physical supply; energy limits qualify continuing provision.','Human-derived engineering agency is explicit, but internal ownership/override rules are not; CentreBrain is not assumed sovereign merely because it is a supercomputer.','Useful engineering and virtual contributions continue; active uploads are a disclosed proxy and there is no work census.'],[P+'dyson',P+'dyson-guide'],1,proxy=True,alternatives=[5]))
R.append(scoped_record('c0879','per-aspera-supplied-martian-colonies','Per Aspera — AMI-supported human colonies','Per Aspera','Functioning supplied settlements in a continuing human-colonization mission',['game'],
 'Base-game colony mechanics and mission setting','A functioning established colony before any destructive or sovereignty-changing campaign ending','Living human colonists supplied within the selected Martian settlement',
 ['An unimplemented terraforming plan','Failed or deliberately starved colonies','Any campaign ending as inevitable canon','Research points as a nonworking census'],
 'AMI’s industrial network builds and sustains actual human Martian colonies. Established settlements receive food, water or ice, power and habitat infrastructure; their residents contribute research when supplied. The game therefore models an implemented technological support arrangement, not merely a future promise to make Mars habitable. Guarantees are moderately favorable within a functioning maintained settlement, with a broad interval for resource shortages, mission choices and dependence on the controller. No universal Earth welfare system is inferred.\n\nAMI performs operational planning, but Earth-directed mission authority and later branching choices complicate final control. The available references do not settle whether humans can effectively override every sustaining decision at this selected stage, so the control axis remains unresolved and autonomous provision is only a provisional regime interpretation. This point explicitly represents a player-configurable functioning colony state. Human science, care and settlement maintenance remain useful work even when robotic systems supply ordinary materials. Research output and colony capacity do not establish a percentage of all people doing no work, which remains unknown.',
 [-.5,None,None],[[-.85,.25],None,None],
 ['Official mission description and colony mechanics establish actual food, water, power and habitat support; supply and player choices qualify reliability.','AMI operational control coexists with Earth mission direction and branching outcomes; ultimate override authority remains unresolved.','Human research and other useful tasks continue; capacity and research-point output are not all-person participation data.'],[P+'aspera',P+'aspera-research'],5,alternatives=[1]))
